WEBVTT

00:04.421 --> 00:06.923
[intriguing music playing]

00:08.675 --> 00:10.927
[indistinct background chatter, laughter]

00:12.012 --> 00:13.722
BALLAD OF THE HAPPY DESTRUCTION

00:19.936 --> 00:21.938
[Saji] Another perk of our new recruits,

00:22.605 --> 00:25.483
we're finally able to distribute
some free meals.

00:25.984 --> 00:27.986
We don't even have to sell Black Powder.

00:28.069 --> 00:31.531
We have more than enough support
from the wealth of this mansion.

00:32.032 --> 00:34.576
The boss still hasn't come back yet, huh?

00:34.659 --> 00:37.203
No, but it seems
Ton and Natsuki have come back.

00:37.287 --> 00:38.538
They've called a meeting,

00:38.621 --> 00:41.291
'cause apparently,
they've got something to show us.

00:42.167 --> 00:43.209
[growling softly]

00:44.627 --> 00:45.962
[flesh wobbling]

00:46.588 --> 00:48.882
- [grunts]
- [intriguing music playing]

00:48.965 --> 00:49.883
[both gasp]

00:50.717 --> 00:52.886
Amazing. There's not a scratch on her!

00:53.470 --> 00:55.263
That's defense Magic for you.

00:55.346 --> 00:57.891
We may have lost Kikurage
to the En family,

00:57.974 --> 00:59.684
but when she was injured
during the battle,

00:59.768 --> 01:01.770
Natsuki's Magic was awakened.

01:02.395 --> 01:07.067
This thing is like a protective suit.
It may even be able to repel Magic.

01:07.150 --> 01:09.277
[Ton] Yeah! Let's try it next time!

01:09.360 --> 01:10.487
Hang on.

01:10.570 --> 01:13.573
So, if Natsuki can use
Magic as amazing as this,

01:13.656 --> 01:16.284
then, there's no need for her
to stay with the Cross-Eyes.

01:16.868 --> 01:19.788
She can make a good living
with this power, you know?

01:19.871 --> 01:22.749
[Ton] Now that you mention it,
you have a point.

01:26.294 --> 01:27.378
[all gasp]

01:27.462 --> 01:28.630
[Natsuki chuckling]

01:28.713 --> 01:30.381
[Saji] Natsuki, your left eye!

01:30.465 --> 01:33.760
After we returned to the mansion
and healed my arm,

01:34.260 --> 01:36.554
I got this eye tattooed as well.

01:38.473 --> 01:39.891
Listen, guys,

01:39.974 --> 01:44.395
even if I can use Magic now,
I'll always be a member of the Cross-Eyes!

01:46.397 --> 01:47.315
Natsuki...

01:47.982 --> 01:50.902
Yeah, that's just the way I feel about it.

01:51.402 --> 01:53.988
What do you say?
I stay here in the mansion?

01:54.072 --> 01:56.157
Yes, of course you can!

01:56.241 --> 01:59.744
After all, if things get bad,
we might need you around to protect us!

02:00.328 --> 02:02.247
You... you mean it? Oh!

02:02.330 --> 02:03.164
[gasps]

02:03.248 --> 02:04.082
Starting today,

02:04.165 --> 02:06.501
you're a full-fledged member
of the Cross-Eyes.

02:06.584 --> 02:08.002
[gasps] Thanks, Saji.

02:09.003 --> 02:12.006
Thanks, everyone. I won't let you down.

02:13.508 --> 02:15.218
[frantic electronic music playing]

02:27.897 --> 02:29.399
[lyrics in Japanese]

03:40.803 --> 03:41.930
THE BEGINNING

03:42.013 --> 03:42.931
[music fades]

03:47.518 --> 03:48.770
[Nikaido] This is crazy.

03:48.853 --> 03:52.690
I never thought I'd come back
to this mansion, let alone as a man.

03:52.774 --> 03:56.027
[Kawajiri] I gotta say,
you're pretty handsome like this, Nikaido.

03:56.110 --> 03:57.028
[Nikaido chuckles]

03:57.695 --> 04:00.198
You look like
a completely different person.

04:01.908 --> 04:04.827
By the way,
these clothes are really heavy.

04:05.703 --> 04:08.039
[Kawajiri] I used Magic
to make 'em that way.

04:08.122 --> 04:10.208
Your training is still ongoing.

04:10.750 --> 04:14.921
Also, the Magic that powers this disguise
only lasts four hours.

04:15.588 --> 04:19.676
After that, you're gonna return
to your original form, so be careful.

04:20.843 --> 04:23.179
Understood. Four hours...

04:23.888 --> 04:25.473
So, around nine o'clock.

04:28.893 --> 04:31.938
[Kawajiri] A fellow devil once told me
something that could help us.

04:32.772 --> 04:34.983
Apparently, somewhere in this mansion,

04:35.066 --> 04:39.028
there's a room filled solely
with the gifts En received from devils.

04:39.779 --> 04:41.364
Does that ring any bells?

04:41.906 --> 04:42.949
[Nikaido] Mm.

04:43.574 --> 04:45.159
Now that you mention it,

04:45.243 --> 04:47.620
this one time,
En took me to a strange room

04:47.704 --> 04:50.498
and made me listen
to him brag about how cool it was.

04:50.581 --> 04:52.458
Maybe that's the room
you're talking about.

04:52.542 --> 04:54.377
If I remember correctly,

04:54.460 --> 04:57.547
some kind of object
served as a hidden door.

04:58.047 --> 05:01.092
[Kawajiri] Hmm...
All right, let's go look for it.

05:02.093 --> 05:03.303
[intriguing music fades]

05:05.179 --> 05:08.599
Was this room also used
by an En Family officer?

05:08.683 --> 05:10.601
Yeah, this was Noi's room.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.812
Look for anything of monetary value.

05:12.895 --> 05:14.605
Enough with the money already.

05:14.689 --> 05:17.025
So we're looking for information, right?

05:17.108 --> 05:20.486
A clue to where the surviving
En family members might be hiding?

05:21.070 --> 05:23.489
- Hmm...
- [Ton] There sure are a lot of photos.

05:25.450 --> 05:28.953
When the boss gets back,
let's take a group photo together!

05:29.037 --> 05:29.871
Yeah!

05:30.538 --> 05:32.623
I can't wait to put it up here!

05:33.291 --> 05:34.167
[giggles]

05:34.709 --> 05:36.252
[uneasy music playing]

05:36.878 --> 05:38.171
[flies buzzing]

05:39.213 --> 05:42.342
[Risu] Well, well, well,
if it isn't the Cross-Eyes B-squad.

05:42.425 --> 05:43.885
- It's been a while.
- [gasps]

05:43.968 --> 05:45.386
Ri... Risu?!

05:45.470 --> 05:50.099
It's a good thing I held off
erasing these damn tattoos off my face.

05:50.183 --> 05:51.893
I got in here easily.

05:51.976 --> 05:55.480
Now, maybe you've had enough time
to jog your memories.

05:55.980 --> 06:00.902
Risu, it's like I told you before,
none of us have any idea who murdered you.

06:00.985 --> 06:01.944
[Risu] Hmm...

06:02.737 --> 06:08.159
Yeah? Then maybe your beloved Dokuga
is hiding a few things from you guys.

06:08.242 --> 06:09.577
[all gasping]

06:09.660 --> 06:13.039
[Risu] Because he seemed to know
a lot about me.

06:14.499 --> 06:18.753
No worries,
I'll have to ask Dokuga about it myself.

06:19.587 --> 06:21.756
Over our dead bodies, you freak!

06:21.839 --> 06:25.009
[Risu, demonically] Oh yeah?
Just try to stop me, you bastards!

06:25.093 --> 06:26.761
[growling]

06:30.348 --> 06:32.183
[Curse] There it is.

06:32.266 --> 06:33.434
I can feel it...

06:33.935 --> 06:35.937
your murderous intent!

06:36.604 --> 06:37.563
[music stops]

06:40.316 --> 06:41.150
[Aikawa grunts]

06:42.860 --> 06:46.280
Just as I thought,
no guards at this entrance.

06:46.364 --> 06:47.865
[chuckling]

06:48.616 --> 06:51.953
That part-time job for Tanba
paid off after all.

06:53.037 --> 06:55.206
All right, time to find Risu.

06:55.706 --> 06:57.542
[gentle gurgling]

07:04.424 --> 07:07.635
[Tetsujo] Dokuga,
what are you going to do about Natsuki?

07:08.261 --> 07:11.597
If we don't act,
she could be killed, just like Risu was.

07:12.765 --> 07:16.394
[Aikawa] Natsuki might get killed?
What are they talking about?

07:16.477 --> 07:18.396
[pensive music playing]

07:18.479 --> 07:21.774
I mean, how long until
the boss decides he wants her magic?

07:21.858 --> 07:23.901
[Aikawa] Natsuki has Magic?

07:23.985 --> 07:27.071
You're not just gonna sit back
and watch him take it, are you?

07:27.155 --> 07:29.866
We have to stop him!
We need to figure out some way--

07:29.949 --> 07:32.076
I'm thinking about
giving Natsuki a mission.

07:32.160 --> 07:34.203
Something to keep her far away from here.

07:35.329 --> 07:37.582
I'll talk to the boss while she's gone.

07:40.877 --> 07:44.213
I'll ask him
not to kill any more companions.

07:46.674 --> 07:47.675
Tetsujo...

07:49.552 --> 07:51.012
I'm trying so hard.

07:51.596 --> 07:53.723
I want to believe in the boss again.

07:55.266 --> 07:56.476
Dokuga...

08:00.563 --> 08:05.026
No one cared about
some worthless humans like us except him.

08:06.444 --> 08:09.155
When our only option was
to lay down and die,

08:09.238 --> 08:11.491
he gave us a path to keep living.

08:14.118 --> 08:16.704
Hey... You're right, Dokuga.

08:17.371 --> 08:18.748
Let's trust the boss.

08:20.041 --> 08:22.001
I'm sure he'll do the right thing.

08:22.084 --> 08:23.794
[Aikawa] Hmm...

08:28.758 --> 08:31.552
[Nikaido] This whole area
was En's private space.

08:31.636 --> 08:34.764
This is where my bedroom was.
Kikurage's too.

08:34.847 --> 08:36.015
[Kawajiri] I see.

08:36.098 --> 08:38.893
Maybe the room
we're looking for is nearby.

08:38.976 --> 08:40.853
- Who are these guys?
- [tense music playing]

08:40.937 --> 08:43.189
This area is off-limits to non-officers.

08:43.272 --> 08:44.649
Let me handle this.

08:44.732 --> 08:45.942
[Nikaido] Hmm...

08:46.025 --> 08:48.194
I feel like I'm remembering something.

08:48.277 --> 08:49.654
- [Tetsujo] You two.
- [both gasp]

08:49.737 --> 08:51.197
Show me your arms!

08:51.280 --> 08:52.907
I need to check your smoke.

08:52.990 --> 08:56.619
I have a feeling these guys
don't want us poking around here.

08:56.702 --> 08:59.914
I bet they're Cross-Eyes officers.
What do we do?

08:59.997 --> 09:02.416
Come on, hurry up and show me your arms!

09:02.500 --> 09:04.502
[Kawajiri] Use this
as a training opportunity.

09:04.585 --> 09:07.171
You deal with him.
I'll keep searching for the book.

09:07.255 --> 09:09.048
[gasps] Where'd she go? Oh!

09:09.131 --> 09:10.550
[dramatic music playing]

09:10.633 --> 09:11.509
[yelps]

09:11.592 --> 09:14.053
[both grunting]

09:16.597 --> 09:17.515
[Nikaido] Take that!

09:18.349 --> 09:20.142
[Tetsujo grunting]

09:21.227 --> 09:23.271
[Nikaido] My clothes are still heavy!

09:23.354 --> 09:25.273
[grunting]

09:26.315 --> 09:27.733
[Tetsujo] I've got you now!

09:27.817 --> 09:28.734
[Nikaido grunts]

09:28.818 --> 09:30.486
[both straining]

09:37.326 --> 09:39.161
- [Nikaido grunting]
- Oof!

09:42.123 --> 09:43.082
[Tetsujo splutters]

09:43.583 --> 09:45.001
- [music fades]
- [Nikaido sighs]

09:47.086 --> 09:49.505
[groans] Sorry, Dokuga...

09:49.589 --> 09:52.300
Tetsujo, you did well.

09:53.301 --> 09:54.260
Now, you.

09:54.343 --> 09:56.137
- [chuckling]
- [Dokuga] Who are you?

09:56.220 --> 09:57.346
[tense music playing]

09:57.430 --> 10:00.516
[Aikawa] Why are Cross-Eyes
fighting each other?

10:03.519 --> 10:05.354
- [Dokuga grunts]
- [gasps]

10:05.855 --> 10:07.189
He's fast!

10:09.108 --> 10:11.777
Screw training,
this thing is gonna get me killed!

10:11.861 --> 10:13.029
[dramatic music playing]

10:13.112 --> 10:14.572
[seething breath, growls]

10:14.655 --> 10:16.657
[Nikaido grunting]

10:18.534 --> 10:20.536
[pained grunting]

10:24.081 --> 10:25.499
[groans softly]

10:26.375 --> 10:27.335
[pained grunt]

10:28.336 --> 10:29.462
[Nikaido] Ugh!

10:31.005 --> 10:32.131
[Dokuga screaming]

10:33.716 --> 10:35.134
Dokuga! [grunts]

10:35.217 --> 10:37.053
- Huh?
- [Tetsujo grunting]

10:37.136 --> 10:38.888
- [Nikaido grunting]
- [grunts, yelps]

10:41.557 --> 10:42.391
Hmph.

10:42.475 --> 10:44.977
[Tetsujo] Damn it! You bastard!

10:45.478 --> 10:47.521
- You're getting...
-...too cocky!

10:47.605 --> 10:49.023
Huh? Uh...

10:52.610 --> 10:53.527
- [grunts]
- [grunts]

10:55.488 --> 10:58.074
I can't waste all day fighting these guys.
Here's my chance.

10:58.157 --> 11:00.076
- [gasps] Oof!
- [Nikaido grunts]

11:00.576 --> 11:01.702
That hurts...

11:02.995 --> 11:04.080
Ah! You!

11:04.163 --> 11:05.748
[Aikawa] That hurts...

11:05.831 --> 11:08.167
- [strong wind blowing]
- [thunder rumbling]

11:12.672 --> 11:13.923
[Vaux] Hmm...

11:17.093 --> 11:19.762
What the hell
have you been working on over there?

11:20.471 --> 11:22.223
It's Caiman's medical record.

11:22.723 --> 11:24.350
Looking it over,

11:24.433 --> 11:27.603
you can clearly see that deep down,
Caiman is human.

11:28.104 --> 11:32.024
But there's a little abnormality
that's caught my attention.

11:32.983 --> 11:35.444
Well, Caiman is a victim of Magic.

11:35.528 --> 11:38.531
It's only natural there'd be
a few things that are out of place.

11:38.614 --> 11:40.741
That's not what I'm talking about.

11:41.492 --> 11:42.993
How should I put it?

11:43.828 --> 11:45.037
[sighs]

11:45.746 --> 11:49.041
I wish I could talk this over
with Mr. Kasukabe.

11:49.625 --> 11:51.752
If I'm right about this,

11:51.836 --> 11:55.589
we may have found the reason
why Caiman's head regenerates.

11:57.633 --> 12:01.178
I can't believe it's already been
a whole month since then.

12:02.513 --> 12:06.350
I wonder what happened
to Caiman and Nikaido.

12:08.060 --> 12:09.729
QUESTION & ANSWER

12:09.812 --> 12:11.856
[heavy breathing]

12:15.860 --> 12:17.695
He must've come this way to escape.

12:18.195 --> 12:21.073
Damn it! Looks like we lost him.

12:21.157 --> 12:23.033
I hate big houses.

12:23.117 --> 12:25.619
More importantly, Dokuga, are you okay?

12:26.454 --> 12:27.538
[unsteadily] Yeah...

12:28.205 --> 12:31.208
I bet he's at the connecting passage.
Let's go!

12:34.920 --> 12:37.965
All right, it looks like
we managed to shake them off.

12:38.048 --> 12:39.717
- Who the hell are you?
- Huh?

12:39.800 --> 12:43.137
Why do I have to hide together
with a damn Cross-Eye?

12:43.220 --> 12:44.138
[Nikaido grunts]

12:44.722 --> 12:46.891
Come on, you're gonna be in
as much trouble as me

12:46.974 --> 12:48.100
if they find you here.

12:48.184 --> 12:50.936
[gasps] That's it. I remember now!

12:51.020 --> 12:52.855
- It's this stone statue!
- Huh?

12:52.938 --> 12:55.274
Huh, En really thought this through.

12:55.357 --> 12:58.360
He knew no one would wanna
mess with a devil statue.

12:59.153 --> 13:01.363
If I remember correctly...

13:02.031 --> 13:05.367
[Aikawa] Are you sure it's okay
to treat a devil statue like that?

13:06.869 --> 13:07.870
Oh!

13:09.455 --> 13:10.498
Oh wow...

13:10.581 --> 13:13.876
I found it!
The entrance to En's treasure room!

13:13.959 --> 13:17.505
You get in too.
Hide in there until things cool down.

13:17.588 --> 13:19.590
What?! Why do I have to?!

13:19.673 --> 13:21.717
- I'm busy. Whoa!
- Just get... in... the room!

13:21.801 --> 13:23.677
[Aikawa yelping, screaming]

13:23.761 --> 13:25.179
[grunts]

13:25.262 --> 13:26.263
[gasps]

13:26.972 --> 13:27.890
Huh?

13:29.141 --> 13:31.477
What the hell is this place?

13:31.977 --> 13:36.524
This is a top-secret room that En filled
with his most cherished treasures.

13:37.024 --> 13:39.109
Cherished treasures, eh?

13:39.193 --> 13:41.362
Look like a bunch of junk to me.

13:41.445 --> 13:45.407
Also, you haven't told me who you are.
You've been acting like you know me!

13:45.491 --> 13:48.619
Oh! I thought you'd noticed by now.

13:48.702 --> 13:49.787
It's me silly!

13:49.870 --> 13:51.372
I'm Nikaido!

13:51.455 --> 13:54.917
I used Magic to disguise myself
as a man to sneak in here.

13:55.000 --> 13:56.669
What?!

13:56.752 --> 13:59.171
You're telling me you're Nikaido?

13:59.797 --> 14:02.007
You know, now that you mention it...

14:02.508 --> 14:05.928
Just kidding,
I'm not falling for that bullshit. I...

14:06.011 --> 14:08.848
- Ugh...
- Hey, uh, you're hurt pretty bad.

14:08.931 --> 14:11.767
[sighs] Don't worry. It's nothing serious.

14:11.851 --> 14:14.603
- All right, gotta find this book.
- Huh?!

14:16.105 --> 14:18.566
Man, I'm hungry.

14:19.275 --> 14:22.444
Oh, that's right.
I'll eat the curry bread that I brought.

14:22.528 --> 14:24.446
TO EN, CHIDARUMA
A LUCKY DAY IN MARCH

14:24.530 --> 14:26.532
I mean, even if you are Nikaido,

14:26.615 --> 14:29.159
I only met you for the first time
the other day.

14:29.243 --> 14:31.787
I don't even remember your face that well.

14:33.038 --> 14:33.956
- [Nikaido] Oh!
- Hm?

14:34.039 --> 14:36.208
Here it is. This has to be it!

14:36.876 --> 14:38.002
[Aikawa] What's that?

14:38.085 --> 14:40.754
You came all this way
just to steal a stupid book?

14:41.255 --> 14:42.214
Yeah.

14:42.298 --> 14:45.801
This book contains all the information
I need to master my powers...

14:45.885 --> 14:47.219
- [clock bongs]
- [both] Hmm?

14:49.305 --> 14:52.558
- Ah! Oh crap! It's nine o'clock!
- Hmm?

14:59.899 --> 15:01.400
[gulping]

15:07.823 --> 15:10.409
See... I told you

15:12.995 --> 15:14.121
[gulps]

15:14.204 --> 15:16.206
[gasps] Nikaido...

15:18.167 --> 15:19.335
Caiman...

15:20.753 --> 15:23.172
[Aikawa] I told you a million times,

15:23.255 --> 15:26.383
I'm not this "Caiman" guy
you keep talking about.

15:26.884 --> 15:28.510
Jeez, you're annoying!

15:28.594 --> 15:32.389
I guess I did name you Caiman
without much thought about it.

15:33.015 --> 15:36.185
But still... you're telling me
when you transformed back,

15:36.268 --> 15:39.188
you forgot about me, the Hole, the gyoza?

15:39.271 --> 15:41.398
[gasps] Gyoza...

15:41.899 --> 15:44.860
Stop it!
I don't know anything about gyoza!

15:44.944 --> 15:47.905
[man 1] I heard the officers
are fighting a monster in this wing!

15:47.988 --> 15:49.740
- [man 2] Hurry.
- [man 1] Let's take a look!

15:49.823 --> 15:50.991
What's going on?

15:51.492 --> 15:53.702
[indistinct background chatter]

15:53.786 --> 15:55.412
[Saji] Everyone, back off!

15:55.496 --> 15:57.539
It's dangerous! Get back!

15:57.623 --> 15:59.166
Damn it. How pathetic.

15:59.750 --> 16:02.336
[Ton] We can't attack Curse from our side.

16:02.419 --> 16:05.172
We need to think of something
to chase him away.

16:05.255 --> 16:08.968
- Maybe we have to let him talk to Dokuga.
- [Natsuki] Wait, please!

16:10.010 --> 16:11.971
I'll use my Magic to deal with him!

16:12.054 --> 16:13.931
Please, everyone, stay back!

16:14.014 --> 16:14.848
[Saji] Natsuki!

16:14.932 --> 16:15.849
Oh!

16:15.933 --> 16:17.685
That's Natsuki.

16:19.269 --> 16:21.605
What's that black thing over there?

16:21.689 --> 16:22.606
[Aikawa gasps]

16:22.690 --> 16:24.274
- [straining]
- Don't be reckless.

16:24.358 --> 16:27.027
Natsuki,
that cursed bastard never gives up!

16:27.111 --> 16:28.529
[gasps] Wait.

16:28.612 --> 16:32.491
I can't believe it.
Since when can she use Magic?

16:32.574 --> 16:33.534
[Aikawa groans]

16:33.617 --> 16:35.119
[suspenseful music building]

16:35.619 --> 16:37.037
[Aikawa groaning]

16:39.623 --> 16:41.041
[snarls]

16:41.667 --> 16:42.543
[wobbling]

16:43.127 --> 16:46.046
If it comes down to it,
we are not going to let her die.

16:47.172 --> 16:50.050
[Curse] I feel it... I can feel it...

16:50.134 --> 16:52.803
Your murderous intent!

16:52.886 --> 16:54.013
[roars]

16:54.888 --> 16:56.098
[snarling]

16:56.181 --> 16:57.391
[dramatic music playing]

16:59.184 --> 17:00.352
[muffled grunting]

17:00.436 --> 17:01.395
[Curse gasps]

17:03.564 --> 17:05.232
[pained grunting]

17:05.315 --> 17:06.483
Risu!

17:07.818 --> 17:08.652
[Natsuki grunts]

17:08.736 --> 17:10.612
[Curse gasps, snarls]

17:11.196 --> 17:12.156
[seethes]

17:13.323 --> 17:14.616
[Natsuki grunts]

17:14.700 --> 17:16.285
[grunts, splutters]

17:17.077 --> 17:19.496
- [grunts]
- [Curse growling]

17:24.084 --> 17:25.502
[Aikawa] Hmm.

17:25.586 --> 17:28.172
- [whispering] Hey, Nikaido!
- Oh, Asu!

17:28.255 --> 17:29.506
So there you are.

17:29.590 --> 17:31.091
I've caught him!

17:31.175 --> 17:33.927
- All right, way to go, Natsuki!
- You're amazing!

17:34.011 --> 17:37.014
- [Natsuki] What should we do?
- We're gonna hang him outside!

17:38.557 --> 17:39.516
[Curse snarls]

17:40.559 --> 17:41.810
- [Aikawa] Uh...
- Oh! Hey?!

17:41.894 --> 17:42.895
Wait, that guy...

17:42.978 --> 17:45.397
What's wrong? What's all this commotion?

17:46.190 --> 17:47.274
Dokuga!

17:47.357 --> 17:49.985
Risu turned into Curse
and attacked us again!

17:50.069 --> 17:50.903
What?!

17:50.986 --> 17:51.945
It's okay.

17:52.029 --> 17:54.698
Natsuki was able to
take him straight down!

17:54.782 --> 17:58.577
We found out that her Magic
can totally defend against curses!

17:58.660 --> 17:59.912
[Natsuki giggling]

17:59.995 --> 18:01.914
[both gasping]

18:01.997 --> 18:04.166
- [Dokuga] Natsuki, come with us.
- Huh?!

18:04.249 --> 18:05.709
Wait. Why?

18:05.793 --> 18:07.544
[tense music building]

18:07.628 --> 18:08.545
Risu!

18:08.629 --> 18:09.838
Hey! Risu!

18:12.091 --> 18:13.050
[music fades]

18:13.133 --> 18:15.385
[Aikawa straining]

18:16.637 --> 18:18.764
- Oh!
- Risu, get a hold of yourself!

18:18.847 --> 18:21.058
- Wait. Risu was that monster from earlier?
- Hey, Risu!

18:21.642 --> 18:25.270
[whispers] Nikaido, we've got the book.
Time to get out of here.

18:25.354 --> 18:26.313
Oh, right.

18:26.396 --> 18:28.732
[gasps] Hey, aren't you...

18:28.816 --> 18:31.318
It's Kawajiri. Been a while, Aikawa.

18:31.401 --> 18:32.319
[gasps]

18:32.402 --> 18:34.822
[Nikaido] Aikawa,
let's get out of here together.

18:35.447 --> 18:36.365
[Aikawa grunts]

18:36.949 --> 18:38.617
Sorry, but I can't.

18:39.618 --> 18:41.703
Go on without me. [whimpers]

18:43.413 --> 18:45.165
Please, take care of him.

18:45.749 --> 18:47.167
He's my partner.

18:47.668 --> 18:51.296
So, Risu is your partner?
Now I understand.

18:52.047 --> 18:53.465
Got it. Leave it to me.

18:53.966 --> 18:55.592
But what are you going to do?

18:55.676 --> 19:00.347
You've been hiding so many things from me
since the very beginning. What's going on?

19:00.430 --> 19:02.683
- If you could only remember what we--
- [Aikawa groaning]

19:02.766 --> 19:04.726
- [splutters, gasps]
- [Nikaido] Oh!

19:04.810 --> 19:05.978
Oh...

19:06.061 --> 19:08.730
- [Nikaido] What's wrong? Are you okay?
- Don't come near me!

19:08.814 --> 19:10.065
[gasps]

19:10.566 --> 19:13.193
- [Aikawa] Don't come near me!
- [uneasy music playing]

19:13.694 --> 19:16.530
[Nikaido] I know it's your life,
and you can live it however you want,

19:16.613 --> 19:20.033
just... you should come
eat some gyoza sometime.

19:20.868 --> 19:22.744
I'll give you 20% off.

19:24.163 --> 19:26.165
[Aikawa] I can't anymore...

19:27.124 --> 19:28.250
I can't...

19:28.333 --> 19:29.960
[groans] Oh!

19:30.043 --> 19:31.753
Nikaido, let's go!

19:32.880 --> 19:34.089
Oh, Caiman...

19:36.091 --> 19:39.011
- [ominous music playing]
- [Aikawa breathing heavily]

19:46.059 --> 19:47.019
I'm sick of it...

19:47.102 --> 19:48.520
[groaning, retching]

19:48.604 --> 19:50.022
My head!

19:50.105 --> 19:53.525
Ah! I'm sick of it... [retching]

19:53.609 --> 19:57.404
[coughing, retching]

19:58.113 --> 19:59.031
[gasps]

19:59.698 --> 20:01.116
[coughing, retching]

20:01.909 --> 20:03.035
[breathing shakily]

20:03.118 --> 20:04.536
[music continues]

20:06.622 --> 20:08.498
[gasping] I'm sick of it...

20:09.333 --> 20:11.043
[gurgles, retching]

20:11.126 --> 20:12.544
[uneasy music playing]

20:13.086 --> 20:14.546
[Ai] Why fight it?

20:14.630 --> 20:16.590
[labored breathing, gasping]

20:18.300 --> 20:19.551
Shut up...

20:19.635 --> 20:22.054
[Ai] When from the very start...

20:22.137 --> 20:23.764
[spluttering]

20:24.264 --> 20:26.058
[groaning]

20:26.892 --> 20:28.560
[muffled grunting, groaning]

20:30.145 --> 20:32.439
...you never existed.

20:52.793 --> 20:54.169
[uneasy music continues]

21:00.676 --> 21:02.594
[music intensifies]

21:13.563 --> 21:15.440
[padding footsteps squelching]

21:23.740 --> 21:25.617
[choked gagging]

21:33.709 --> 21:35.877
[groaning]

21:35.961 --> 21:37.170
[music fades]

21:39.631 --> 21:43.218
[Natsuki squeals excitedly] Yay!
A mission, a mission!

21:43.844 --> 21:47.806
I can't believe Dokuga is letting me
do a job all by myself.

21:47.889 --> 21:49.224
[giggling happily]

21:50.183 --> 21:53.478
Hmm... So it's a search
for an elite Sorcerer.

21:53.562 --> 21:55.522
EN'S MANSION, DOG, CONVENIENCE STORE
FOREST, TARGET

21:55.605 --> 21:56.982
It's pretty far away.

21:57.065 --> 22:01.153
I wanted the boss to at least see my Magic
before I set out.

22:01.236 --> 22:02.487
[tense music playing]

22:03.405 --> 22:05.574
But they told to leave
through the back door

22:05.657 --> 22:06.992
so no one would notice.

22:07.075 --> 22:08.785
I wonder why?

22:11.955 --> 22:12.998
[Natsuki gasps]

22:13.081 --> 22:14.499
The boss!

22:15.417 --> 22:17.794
I... I, uh... Oh?

22:18.462 --> 22:19.296
Huh?

22:19.379 --> 22:20.213
[squeals]

22:20.297 --> 22:23.717
I... I'm about to start a mission!

22:23.800 --> 22:26.470
Um, s... so I, uh...

22:26.553 --> 22:30.307
When I get back, I want all the Cross-Eyes
to take a picture together--

22:30.390 --> 22:31.224
Whoa!

22:34.061 --> 22:35.812
I want you...

22:36.313 --> 22:37.689
Oh, Boss...

22:38.690 --> 22:39.733
- [kissing]
- [muffled grunt]

22:45.822 --> 22:48.241
- [boss growling softly]
- [Natsuki whimpering]

22:50.202 --> 22:51.078
[muffled wail]

22:51.578 --> 22:52.704
[gasps]

22:53.205 --> 22:54.498
[spluttering] B... Boss...

22:55.749 --> 22:57.334
[weakly] W... why?

23:01.463 --> 23:04.591
[ragged exhaling]

23:21.942 --> 23:24.903
[ominous whirring]

23:24.986 --> 23:26.822
[Japanese theme song playing]

24:53.658 --> 24:54.951
THE END

24:55.035 --> 24:56.870
[narrator] What we learned in Episode 23.

24:56.953 --> 24:59.164
There was a major clue
in Caiman's medical record.

24:59.247 --> 25:01.208
Aikawa entrusted Risu to Nikaido.

25:01.291 --> 25:03.668
Natsuki wanted to take
a picture with everyone.

25:03.752 --> 25:07.589
What we're going to learn in Episode 24,
it's still lost in chaos.

25:07.672 --> 25:09.883
This is Dorohedoro!
